buting/how-to-release","content":"Apache Phoenix release process, release candidates, and voting workflow."},"216":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-1","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#contributing-how-to-release","content":"How to Release"},"217":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-2","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#pre-reqs","content":"Pre-Reqs"},"218":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-3","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"Do a dry run"},"219":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-4","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#create-real-rc","content":"Create real RC"},"220":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-5","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#close-the-staging-repository","content":"Close the staging repository"},"221":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-6","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#voting","content":"Voting"},"222":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-7","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Release"},"223":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-8","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#contributing-how-to-release","content":"Phoenix has several repos: phoenix-thirdparty, phoenix-omid, phoenix-tephra, phoenix, phoenix-connectors, and phoenix-queryserver.\nThe create-release scripts provide a unified script to handle the release from each repo.\nThe create-release scripts are in the master branch of the phoenix repo, in the dev/create-release directory."},"224":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-9","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#pre-reqs","content":"Make sure that the JIRAs included in the release have their fix-version and release notes fields set correctly, and are resolved.The script will query them and create the CHANGES and RELEASE_NOTES files from that information.Use dev/misc_utils/git_jira_fix_version_check.py to find discrepancies between commits and JIRAs."},"225":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-10","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#pre-reqs","content":"Make sure you have set up your user for release signing. Details: http://www.apache.org/dev/release-signing.html."},"226":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-11","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#pre-reqs","content":"Make sure you have set up Maven for deploying to the ASF repo. Details: https://infra.apache.org/publishing-maven-artifacts.html."},"227":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-12","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#pre-reqs","content":"Clone the Phoenix master branch locally (the script will download the actual repo to release itself)."},"228":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-13","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#pre-reqs","content":"Make sure Docker is running locally."},"229":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-14","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#pre-reqs","content":"Note that Docker Desktop for Mac works, but will be slow (several hours for a Phoenix core release). Running on a native Linux machine is much faster because you avoid filesystem translation layer overhead."},"230":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-15","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"Read /dev/create_release/README.txt to understand what the script does and how to set up gpg-agent for signing."},"231":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-16","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"Run the dev/create-release/do-release-docker.sh -d <workdir> -p <project> command, where"},"232":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-17","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"<project> is the repo name you're releasing from (i.e. phoenix)"},"233":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-18","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"<workdir> is any existing directory that can be deleted"},"234":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-19","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"The script will ask a number of questions. Some of them will have intelligent default, but make sure you check them all:"},"235":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-20","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"PROJECT: the repo to release (default specified by -p on the command line)"},"236":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-21","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"GIT_BRANCH: the git branch to use for release. This can be master, or a pre-created release branch."},"237":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-22","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"RC_COUNT: the RC number, starting from 0"},"238":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-23","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"RELEASE_TAG: the git tag the script will tag the RC commit with."},"239":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-24","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"ASF_USERNAME: your ASF username, for publishing the release artifacts."},"240":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-25","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"ASF_PASSWORD: your ASF password, only for non-dry runs"},"241":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-26","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"GIT_NAME/GIT_EMAIL: will be used for the RC commit"},"242":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-27","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"GPG_KEY: ID for your GPG key. The script will offer a GPG secret key from your key ring, double-check that it is your code-signing key, and correct it if it is not."},"243":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-28","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#do-a-dry-run","content":"The dry-run will generate the signed release files into <workdir>/output directory.\nThe Maven artifacts will be in <workdir>/output/phoenix-repo-XXXX local Maven repo, in the usual structure."},"244":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-29","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#create-real-rc","content":"If the dry-run release artifacts (source, binary, and Maven) check out, then publish a real RC to ASF."},"245":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-30","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#create-real-rc","content":"Repeat the dry run process, but add the -f switch to the do-release-docker.sh command."},"246":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-31","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#create-real-rc","content":"The script will upload the source and binary release artifacts to a directory under https://dist.apache.org/repos/dist/dev/phoenix/.\nThe script will also deploy the Maven artifacts to https://repository.apache.org/#stagingRepositories.\nCheck that these are present."},"247":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-32","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#close-the-staging-repository","content":"The published staging repository is in the \"open\" state. Open staging repositories\nare aggressively cleaned up, and may be removed by the time the vote passes.\nTo avoid this, close\n(but DO NOT release) the staging repository immediately after deployment."},"248":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-33","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#voting","content":"Initiate the vote email. See example here, or use the <workdir>/output/vote.txt template generated by the script."},"249":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-34","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#voting","content":"In case the RC (Release Candidate) is rejected via the vote, you will have to repeat the above process and re-initiate the vote for the next RC (RC0, RC1, etc.)."},"250":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-35","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Once voting is successful (say for RC1), copy artifacts to https://dist.apache.org/repos/dist/release/phoenix:"},"251":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-36","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Set release tag and commit:"},"252":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-37","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Remove any obsolete releases on https://dist.apache.org/repos/dist/release/phoenix given the current release."},"253":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-38","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Go to https://repository.apache.org/#stagingRepositories and release the staged artifacts (this takes a while so you may need to refresh multiple times)."},"254":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-39","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Create new branch based on current release if needed, for ex: 4.15 branches in this case."},"255":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-40","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Set version to the upcoming SNAPSHOT and commit:"},"256":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-41","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"If releasing Phoenix (core) Create a JIRA to update PHOENIX_MAJOR_VERSION, PHOENIX_MINOR_VERSION and PHOENIX_PATCH_NUMBER in MetaDataProtocol.java appropriately to next version (4, 16, 0 respectively in this case) and compatible_client_versions.json file with the client versions that are compatible against the next version (in this case 4.14.3 and 4.15.0 would be the backward compatible clients for 4.16.0). This JIRA should be committed/marked with fixVersion of the next release candidate."},"257":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-42","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Add documentation of released version to the downloads page and wiki."},"258":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-43","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Update the Apache Committee Report Helper DB"},"259":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-44","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Send out an announcement email. See example here."},"260":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-45","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Bulk close JIRAs that were marked for the release fixVersion."},"261":{"id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release-46","page_id":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing/how-to-release#release","content":"Congratulations!"},"262":{"id":"/docs/contributing","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"page","content":"Contributing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Multi-Page Documentation","Development","Contributing"],"tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing"},"263":{"id":"/docs/contributing-0","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing","content":"Contribution workflow for Apache Phoenix, including JIRA, patch/PR submission, and committer practices."},"264":{"id":"/docs/contributing-1","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"General process"},"265":{"id":"/docs/contributing-2","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#discuss-on-the-mailing-list","content":"Discuss on the mailing list"},"266":{"id":"/docs/contributing-3","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#log-a-jira-ticket","content":"Log a JIRA ticket"},"267":{"id":"/docs/contributing-4","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#setup-development-environment","content":"Setup development environment"},"268":{"id":"/docs/contributing-5","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#generate-a-patch","content":"Generate a patch"},"269":{"id":"/docs/contributing-6","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#naming-convention-for-the-patch","content":"Naming convention for the patch"},"270":{"id":"/docs/contributing-7","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#github-workflow","content":"GitHub workflow"},"271":{"id":"/docs/contributing-8","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#local-git-workflow","content":"Local Git workflow"},"272":{"id":"/docs/contributing-9","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#code-conventions","content":"Code conventions"},"273":{"id":"/docs/contributing-10","page_id":"/docs/contributing","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/contributing#committer-workflow","content":"Committer workflow"},"274":{"id":"/docs/contributing-11","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"The general process for contributing code to Phoenix works as follows:"},"275":{"id":"/docs/contributing-12","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"Discuss your changes on the dev mailing list"},"276":{"id":"/docs/contributing-13","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"Create a JIRA issue unless there already is one"},"277":{"id":"/docs/contributing-14","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"Setup your development environment"},"278":{"id":"/docs/contributing-15","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"Prepare a patch containing your changes"},"279":{"id":"/docs/contributing-16","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"Submit the patch"},"280":{"id":"/docs/contributing-17","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"These steps are explained in greater detail below."},"281":{"id":"/docs/contributing-18","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#general-process","content":"Note that the instructions below are for the main Phoenix project.\nUse the corresponding repository for the other subprojects.\nTephra and Omid also have their own JIRA projects."},"282":{"id":"/docs/contributing-19","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#discuss-on-the-mailing-list","content":"It's often best to discuss a change on the public mailing lists before creating and submitting a patch."},"283":{"id":"/docs/contributing-20","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#discuss-on-the-mailing-list","content":"If you're unsure whether certain behavior in Phoenix is a bug, please send a mail to the user mailing list to check."},"284":{"id":"/docs/contributing-21","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#discuss-on-the-mailing-list","content":"If you're considering adding major new functionality to Phoenix, it's a good idea to first discuss the idea on the developer mailing list to make sure that your plans are in line with others in the Phoenix community."},"285":{"id":"/docs/contributing-22","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#log-a-jira-ticket","content":"The first step is to create a ticket on the Phoenix JIRA."},"286":{"id":"/docs/contributing-23","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#setup-development-environment","content":"To set up your development environment, see these directions."},"287":{"id":"/docs/contributing-24","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#generate-a-patch","content":"There are two general approaches for creating and submitting a patch: GitHub pull requests, or manual patch creation with Git. Both are explained below. Please make sure that the patch applies cleanly on all active branches, including master and the unified 4.x branch."},"288":{"id":"/docs/contributing-25","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#generate-a-patch","content":"Regardless of which approach is taken, please make sure to follow the Phoenix code conventions (more information below). Whenever possible, unit tests or integration tests should be included with patches."},"289":{"id":"/docs/contributing-26","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#generate-a-patch","content":"Please make sure that the patch contains only one commit, then click the \"Submit patch\" button to automatically trigger tests on the patch."},"290":{"id":"/docs/contributing-27","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#generate-a-patch","content":"The commit message should reference the JIRA ticket issue (which has the format\nPHOENIX-{NUMBER}:{JIRA-TITLE})."},"291":{"id":"/docs/contributing-28","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#generate-a-patch","content":"To effectively get the patch reviewed, please raise the pull request against an appropriate branch."},"292":{"id":"/docs/contributing-29","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#naming-convention-for-the-patch","content":"When generating a patch, make sure the patch name uses the following format:\nPHOENIX-{NUMBER}.{BRANCH-NAME}.{VERSION}.patch"},"293":{"id":"/docs/contributing-30","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#naming-convention-for-the-patch","content":"Examples: PHOENIX-4872.master.v1.patch, PHOENIX-4872.master.v2.patch, PHOENIX-4872.4.x-HBase-1.3.v1.patch, etc."},"294":{"id":"/docs/contributing-31","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#github-workflow","content":"Create a pull request in GitHub for the mirror of the Phoenix Git repository."},"295":{"id":"/docs/contributing-32","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#github-workflow","content":"Generate a patch and attach it to JIRA so Hadoop QA runs automated tests."},"296":{"id":"/docs/contributing-33","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#github-workflow","content":"If you update the PR, generate a new patch with a different name so patch changes are detected and tests run for the new patch."},"297":{"id":"/docs/contributing-34","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#local-git-workflow","content":"Create a local branch:"},"298":{"id":"/docs/contributing-35","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#local-git-workflow","content":"Make and commit changes"},"299":{"id":"/docs/contributing-36","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#local-git-workflow","content":"Generate a patch based on the JIRA issue number:"},"300":{"id":"/docs/contributing-37","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#local-git-workflow","content":"Attach the created patch file to the JIRA ticket."},"301":{"id":"/docs/contributing-38","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#code-conventions","content":"The Phoenix code conventions are similar to the Sun/Oracle Java Code Convention. We use 4 spaces (no tabs) for indentation and limit lines to 100 characters."},"302":{"id":"/docs/contributing-39","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#code-conventions","content":"Eclipse code formatting settings and import order settings (which can also be imported into Intellij IDEA) are available in the dev directory of the Phoenix codebase."},"303":{"id":"/docs/contributing-40","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#code-conventions","content":"All new source files should include the Apache license header."},"304":{"id":"/docs/contributing-41","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#committer-workflow","content":"In general, the \"rebase\" workflow should be used with the Phoenix codebase (see this blog post for more information on the difference between \"merge\" and \"rebase\" workflows in Git)."},"305":{"id":"/docs/contributing-42","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#committer-workflow","content":"A patch file can be downloaded from a GitHub pull request by adding .patch to the end of the pull request URL, for example: https://github.com/apache/phoenix/pull/35.patch."},"306":{"id":"/docs/contributing-43","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#committer-workflow","content":"When applying a user-contributed patch, use git am when a fully formatted patch file is available, as this preserves contributor contact information. Otherwise, add the contributor's name to the commit message."},"307":{"id":"/docs/contributing-44","page_id":"/docs/contributing","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/contributing#committer-workflow","content":"If a single ticket consists of a patch with multiple commits, the commits can be squashed into a single commit using git rebase."},"308":{"id":"/docs/datatypes","page_id":"/docs/datatypes","type":"page","content":"Data Types","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Multi-Page Documentation","Reference"],"tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/datatypes"},"309":{"id":"/docs/datatypes-0","page_id":"/docs/datatypes","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"tex