permission-issues-when-uploading-hfiles","content":"The first option can be done by running:"},"725":{"id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading-69","page_id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/bulk-loading#permission-issues-when-uploading-hfiles","content":"Creating output files readable by all can be done by setting fs.permissions.umask-mode to 000. This can be set in Hadoop config on the submit host, or only for job submission:"},"726":{"id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading-70","page_id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/bulk-loading#loading-array-data","content":"Both PSQL and MapReduce loaders support array values with -a. Arrays in CSV are represented by a field that uses a different delimiter than the main CSV delimiter. For example, this file represents an id field and an array of integers:"},"727":{"id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading-71","page_id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/bulk-loading#loading-array-data","content":"To load this file, use the default CSV delimiter (comma) and pass colon as the array delimiter via -a ':'."},"728":{"id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading-72","page_id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/bulk-loading#a-note-on-separator-characters","content":"The default separator for both loaders is comma (,). A common separator for input files is tab, which can be tricky to pass on the command line. A common mistake is:"},"729":{"id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading-73","page_id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/bulk-loading#a-note-on-separator-characters","content":"This does not work because the shell passes two characters (backslash and t) to Phoenix."},"730":{"id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading-74","page_id":"/docs/features/bulk-loading","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/feature