client metrics emitted by PQS in hadoop-metrics2.properties."},"1209":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-171","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#query-server-metrics-config","content":"FAT_CLIENT"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-172","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#query-server-additions","content":"The Phoenix Query Server is meant to be horizontally scalable which means that it\nis a natural fit for add-on features like service discovery and load balancing."},"1211":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-173","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"The Query Server can use off-the-shelf HTTP load balancers such as the Apache HTTP Server,\nnginx, or HAProxy. The primary requirement of\nusing these load balancers is that the implementation must implement \"sticky session\" (when a client\ncommunicates with a backend server, that client continues to talk to that backend server). The Query Server also\nprovides some bundled functionality for load balancing using ZooKeeper."},"1212":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-174","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"The ZooKeeper-based load balancer functions by automatically registering PQS instances in\nZooKeeper and then allows clients to query the list of available servers. This implementation, unlike\nthe others mentioned above, requires that client use the advertised information to make a routing decision.\nIn this regard, this ZooKeeper-based approach is more akin to a service-discovery layer than a traditional\nload balancer. This load balancer implementation does not support SASL-based (Kerberos) ACLs in\nZooKeeper (see PHOENIX-4085)."},"1213":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-175","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"The following properties configure this load balancer:"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-176","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"Property"},"1215":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-177","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"Description"},"1216":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-178","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"Default"},"1217":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-179","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"phoenix.queryserver.loadbalancer.enabled"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-180","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"If true, PQS registers itself in ZooKeeper for load balancing."},"1219":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-181","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"false"},"1220":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-182","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"phoenix.queryserver.base.path"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-183","page_id":"/docs/features/query-server","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/features/query-server#load-balancing","content":"Root znode where PQS instances register themselves."},"1222":{"id":"/docs/features/query-server-184","page_id":"/docs/feat